  "body": "## What changed\n\nThis change is **view only** (a display transform of the reference furniture). It does not move a stored body.\n\n- The new `crates/ui/src/floor.rs` gives `floor_z`. This is the lowest finite world Z of the drawn bodies:\n  - the models (a model hidden by its eye counts too, so the floor does not jump),\n  - the fixtures of the shown setups,\n  - the stock of the active setup.\n- The ground grid (`interact::ground_grid_lines`) is drawn at the floor, not at world Z=0.\n- The bottom of a mill work envelope box (`work_envelope::envelope_lines`) stands on the floor. The box keeps its full Z travel (#1963).\n- With no fixture, the model and the stock stand on the floor. A fixture under the stock puts the floor at the fixture base, so the model and the stock stand on the fixture. When you remove the fixture, the floor comes back up to the stock.\n- The floor is read from the world at each frame, so undo and redo follow it. No new command and no MCP tool are necessary.\n- A lathe frame (#1993) keeps the floor at world Z=0. A floor that is not finite or is past 1e7 mm falls back to 0.\n- The tooltip of \"Show work envelope\" now says that the boxes stand on the floor under the model, the stock and the fixtures.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/2172-viewport-floor.md`. The dropped alternative is a stored \"lift\" command. That command can change posted coordinates when a WCS is at a world position, so it is under the safety floor.\n\n## Safety result\n\nNo file in `crates/app`, `post`, `sim` or `cl` changes. The WCS still comes from the setup. Stored poses, toolpaths, collision checks, simulation, carried stock and the posted program read the world, and the world does not change. A test pins this.\n\n## Readings\n\n- A 20 x 20 x 30 block, centred on the origin: floor = -15 (before: grid at 0, half of the block below it).\n- After a stock fit (margin 2): floor = -17 (the stock bottom).\n- After a 6 in vise is placed under the stock: the floor is the vise base. The stock bottom is at the vise frame Z, above the floor.\n\n## Pinning tests (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/floor.rs`)\n\n- `a_loaded_model_has_its_lowest_point_on_the_floor`\n- `a_created_fixture_stands_on_the_floor_and_lifts_the_model_and_stock`\n- `removing_the_fixture_drops_the_bodies_back_and_undo_redo_restore_each_state`\n- `the_floor_never_changes_the_posted_records_or_the_checks` (the record stream from `posting::stream_records` and the `posting::verification_gate` findings are the same before and after all floor readers and `world::collect` run; stored poses are the same)\n- The updated `work_envelope` library test asserts the bottom at `floor_z` and the top at floor + travel.\n\n## Gate\n\n- `camcraft-ui` lib suite: 936 passed, 1 failed, 6 ignored. The failure is `stock_fit_controls_follow_the_selected_shape`. It also fails on main (#2170, fix in PR #2171).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No pixel snapshot is changed or run (release lane).\n- I did not open the GUI. There is no before/after screenshot yet.\n- The test does not compare the full written G-code file of the seeded document. The seeded program fails the verification gate (holder contact), so `post_setup_unwritten` refuses it. The test compares the record stream that the post engine translates.\n\nChangelog: The viewport grid and the work envelope now stand on the lowest point of the model, the stock and the fixtures, so a model no longer shows half under the floor. Display only: posted programs do not change.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2172\n\n## Screenshots\n\nA test machine with its work envelope shown. The camera is the same in all six images.\n\n| Scene | Before (main) | After (this PR) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Model alone | ![before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/447928912568498b758982375334f115e5fe5662/pr-2175/before-a-model.png) | ![after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/447928912568498b758982375334f115e5fe5662/pr-2175/after-a-model.png) |\n| Vise fixture created | ![before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/447928912568498b758982375334f115e5fe5662/pr-2175/before-b-vise.png) | ![after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/447928912568498b758982375334f115e5fe5662/pr-2175/after-b-vise.png) |\n| Fixture removed | ![before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/447928912568498b758982375334f115e5fe5662/pr-2175/before-c-removed.png) | ![after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/447928912568498b758982375334f115e5fe5662/pr-2175/after-c-removed.png) |\n\nBefore: the grid cuts through the model and the vise. After: the grid and the envelope bottom are at the lowest point, and the bodies stand on it.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
